{
  "pluginName": "ModForgeSkillTree.esp",
  "esl": true,

  "_comment": "Idea #20 Phase 1 (STANDALONE, ZERO external-mod dependency) — a self-contained in-world skill tree needing only Skyrim.esm (NO Campfire/Frostfall INSTALLED). Uses Campfire's FLOATING STAR mesh (_camp_intperkstars01.nif) — but BUNDLED as a loose asset (assets/skilltree/), not via Campfire.esm. That mesh's textures are ALL vanilla (it reuses the vanilla perk-constellation star textures interface\\INTPerkStars01.dds + effects\\gradients\\GradIntStars.dds etc.), so only the .nif ships. The star floats (its havok collision is fixed/keyframed for click-detection, NOT dynamic — unlike the WispCrystal first attempt that fell). 3 floating star nodes stacked vertically in the Whiterun Bannered Mare; click one -> our MFSkillNode.psc gate-checks (prerequisite node + points) -> grants a custom Fortify ability + spends a point. Chain: Forged Resolve (root) -> Forged Vigor -> Forged Mastery. TEST: `coc WhiterunBanneredMare`, look for 3 stacked glowing stars, click the lowest.",

  "assets": "assets/skilltree",

  "globals": [
    { "editorId": "MFSkill_PointsAvail", "type": "short", "value": 3, "_": "shared point pool; starts at 3 so you can buy all three immediately for the test" },
